[38;2;124;124;124mThe question is whether $\int_{\{u>0\}} u = \int_{\{u<0\}} |u|$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThese are different conditions in general. The first weights by $u^{q-2}$ (power[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$q-2$ of $u$), the second is unweighted.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor $q = 2$: $|u|^{q-2}u = |u|^0 u = u$. So the condition becomes $\int u = 0$, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mwhich trivially implies $\int u = 0$. So for $q = 2$ it's trivially true.[0m

